course: dictionary
lesson: 1633
title: A tree sap that became gum
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can connect a science lesson to everyday life. Chicle is a noun, and it is a natural gum. Its meaning is in the first part of this sentence: «Chewing gum is a rubbery gum base kneaded with sugar or sweetener and flavour.» Gum base is the rubbery part that makes gum chewy, and chicle was one of the natural ones.
explain: The sentence also says, «long ago people chewed a tree sap called chicle.» Long ago tells you this happened in the past, and a tree sap is the sticky liquid inside a tree. So chicle is a gum that people once got from a tree, not one made in a factory.
explain: The next clue is «most gum base today is made in factories.» The word today shows a change: modern gum usually uses a man-made gum base, not chicle. When you read about a thing that has changed over time, look for words like long ago, today, and now.
fact: Chicle is a natural gum made from the milky sap of the sapodilla tree.
fact: The sapodilla tree grows in Central America.
fact: The Maya and Aztec peoples chewed chicle long ago.
fact: Chewing gum companies in the USA later used chicle to make gum.
fact: Most modern gum is made from a synthetic gum base, made in factories, not from chicle.
exercise: «Long ago people chewed a tree sap called chicle.» What is chicle? | Dried mud from a river bank | *A natural gum from the milky sap of a tree | A kind of plastic toy | A sweet made from sugar and flavour
exercise: Where does chicle come from? | An oak tree in England | A palm tree on a desert island | *A sapodilla tree in Central America | A pine tree in Canada
exercise: «Most gum base today is made in factories.» What does the word today tell you? | Gum is always made from trees | *Modern gum usually does not use chicle | Chicle is still the only gum base | Factories were built long ago
test: Which peoples chewed chicle long ago? | Inuit and Sami peoples | *Maya and Aztec peoples | Egyptians and Greeks | Vikings and Romans
test: «Chewing gum is a rubbery gum base kneaded with sugar or sweetener and flavour.» Which word tells you that chewing gum is rubbery and chewy? | *rubbery | flavour | factories | sugar
exam: Why is chicle a good example of a word that links science to everyday life? | *It is a natural sap from a tree, and it connects plant science with the gum people chew every day | It means a type of car engine | It is a plant sap from a real tree, and it was used to make the gum people chew | It is a word only used in maths lessons
